{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 1, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 14873453856302570034, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {".pytest_cache/.gitignore": {"bytes": 37, "mtime": 1792282105.2957864, "sha256": "3ed731b65d06150c138e2dadb0be0697550888a6b47eb8c45ecc9adba8b8e9bd"}, ".pytest_cache/CACHEDIR.TAG": {"bytes": 191, "mtime": 1792282105.2957864, "sha256": "37dc88ef9a0abeddbe81053a6dd8fdfb13afb613045ea1eb4a5c815a74a3bde4"}, ".pytest_cache/README.md": {"bytes": 302, "mtime": 1792282105.2957864, "sha256": "73fd6fccdd802c419a6b2d983d6c3173b7da97558ac4b589edec2dfe443db9ad"}, ".pytest_cache/v/cache/nodeids": {"bytes": 39, "mtime": 1792282105.2957864, "sha256": "c29bed0349cb6e5f8b85c1482b32707cc5f4eeb5906b15211b628f9e00f20138"}, "pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1792267701.6326475, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 565, "mtime": 1792282104.9957864, "sha256": "5414e970e42771fe2a01af533b204cf298e2503af7034244597f0f589ade86fe"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1792267701.6326475, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step4-omp-sonnet-1017/omp-38/transcripts/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/19/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step4-omp-sonnet-1017/omp-38/cells/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/19/workspace", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "with", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`. The fix is in `pricing/money.py`.\n\n**Cause:** the old code used `round(x, 2)`, which rounds the float's binary value. `2.675` is stored as roughly `2.67499999\u2026`, so it rounded down.\n\n**Fix:** `round_money` now converts the value with `repr(x)` into a `Decimal`, then rounds to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. The function still returns a float.\n\n**Checks:** I ran these by hand, and the existing test in `tests/test_split.py` still passes.\n- `2.675` gives `2.68`.\n- `1.005` gives `1.01`.\n- `2.5` gives `2.5`.\n- `3` gives `3.0`.\n- `add_vat(10)` gives `12.0`.\n- `-2.675` gives `-2.68`, because ties round away from zero.\n\nI didn't add a test for `round_money` itself.\n\n**Remaining risk:** the fix relies on the float's shortest repr being the decimal the customer meant. If an upstream calculation produces noise like `2.6749999999999998`, it will still round down. `add_vat` multiplies floats, so this is possible there. Using `Decimal` for prices end to end would remove that risk, but it's a bigger change than you asked for.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 4, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 109020, "requests_cache_